4. Mathematical Foundations

4.1 Retrieval with Multi‑Signal Cognitive Scoring

Pure cosine similarity is insufficient for personal memory. Private Guardian uses a four‑signal composite score, validated by SmartVector and Neural Long Memory:

\text{score}(m_i, q, t) = \alpha \cdot \text{cos}(\mathbf{q}, \mathbf{m}_i) + \beta \cdot \text{decay}(t - t_i) + \gamma \cdot \rho(m_i) + \delta \cdot \frac{\log(1 + a_i)}{\log(1 + A_{\max})}

where decay follows a hybrid exponential/power‑law model (Ebbinghaus, 1885; Wixted, 2004) reflecting short‑term exponential forgetting and long‑term power‑law retention.

4.2 Three‑Domain Key Hierarchy

All encryption keys are derived from the master key \mathcal{K}_{\text{master}} via HKDF (RFC 5869):

\begin{aligned}
\mathcal{K}_{\text{cat}} &= \text{HKDF}(\mathcal{K}_{\text{master}}, \text{"category:"} \| \text{id}) \\
\mathcal{K}_{\text{backup}} &= \text{HKDF}(\mathcal{K}_{\text{master}}, \text{"ghost\_backup"}) \\
\mathcal{K}_{\text{transport}}^{(i)} &= \text{HKDF}(\mathcal{K}_{\text{backup}}, \text{"transport:"} \| i)
\end{aligned}

Memory entries are encrypted with AES‑256‑GCM using position‑derived nonces, guaranteeing uniqueness.

4.3 Append‑Only Journal Integrity

The Black Box maintains a Balloon‑inspired log: each entry L_i = (E_i, h_i, \sigma_i, t_i) with h_i = \text{SHA‑3‑256}(h_{i-1} \| E_i \| t_i \| i). Forward security ensures that no pre‑compromise entry can be modified undetectably.

4.4 Shamir Ghost Sharding

Given an encrypted bundle E, a random polynomial P(x) = E + a_1 x + a_2 x^2 over \mathbb{F}_q generates 5 shares. Reconstruction via Lagrange interpolation requires 3 shares. Secrecy is information‑theoretic: fewer than 3 shares reveal nothing.

4.5 Memory Aging and Consensual Forgetting

Retention weight decays via the hybrid model, with a two‑threshold policy: memories below the hot threshold migrate to Ghost cold storage; those below the cold threshold are flagged for deletion, subject to user confirmation.

