8. Conclusion

This thesis has presented Private Guardian—a rigorous, formal architectural design for a sovereign AI companion that separates active cognition from permanent, physically isolated memory. By integrating local‑first inference, a cryptographically hardened Black Box, minimal‑disclosure cognitive access, and the Ghost Backup for disaster resilience, the system demonstrates that deep personalisation, lifelong continuity, and absolute user sovereignty are technically achievable. All necessary cryptographic and algorithmic primitives are available today. The architecture stands as a blueprint for a future where AI companions remember without surveilling, and where the most intimate data of a human life remains irreversibly in the hands of the one who lived it.

