The following metrics are defined as formal targets. No empirical measurements have been made; the values are derived from published benchmarks of the underlying primitives (Qdrant HNSW latency, Shamir computational cost, LLM token generation rates on listed hardware). They are provided as a verification framework for a future prototype.

Metric Description Formal Target Basis
P1 Plaintext egress rate 0 bytes/day Architectural invariant
P2 Robot compromise exposure window ≤ 24 hours Consolidation interval bound
P3 Category key isolation Proven by HKDF security RFC 5869
P4 Cloud semantic obliviousness 0 bits beyond share size Information‑theoretic secrecy of Shamir (t=3)
C1 Hot‑tier retrieval precision@1 ≥ 0.60 SmartVector reported 0.62 for similar four‑signal score
C3‑hot End‑to‑end hot‑tier latency ≤ 500 ms HNSW search 1.8 ms (Qdrant) + LLM inference ≤ 200 ms per token on Jetson
C3‑cold Cold‑tier reconstruction latency ≤ 120 s Lagrange interpolation O(t²) + AES decryption + network round‑trip
S1 Consolidation throughput ≤ 60 s/day Projected from compression ratio and journal write bandwidth
S2 Shard generation overhead ≤ 30 s for 1 GB Projected from SSS arithmetic over \mathbb{F}_{2^{256}}
U1 Key recovery success (planned) ≥ 95 % in simulated loss scenarios Shamir threshold scheme with backup shares

This framework constitutes the prospective validation contract for Private Guardian. It demonstrates that the architecture makes specific, falsifiable claims, even in the absence of a current implementation.

